    {
      "id": "p0160-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In English, Aaron often ends his text with ;), which is a common Western emoticon of someone winking. Japanese emoticons are generally quite different, however, so the original winking face was replaced with a Japanese-style winking face: (^_-)☆",
        "raw": "In English, Aaron often ends his text with;), which is a common Western\nemoticon of someone winking. Japanese emoticons are generally quite\ndifferent, however, so the original winking face was replaced with a Japanese\nstyle winking face: (\"'_-)-tr",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
